nightshift tree"}},{"tool_name":"Read","tool_use_id":"toolu_01P37ag39XKJUse4keaoHbBT","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/Rushi/.claude/plugins/cache/nightshift/sdlc/0.45.4/commands/auto.md"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cj4BF3fVaHwJTn7AKomDcx","tool_input":{"command":"rtk diff -q plugins/sdlc/commands/auto.md /Users/Rushi/.claude/plugins/cache/nightshift/sdlc/0.45.4/commands/auto.md 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\"; rtk wc -l plugins/sdlc/commands/auto.md /Users/Rushi/.claude/plugins/cache/nightshift/sdlc/0.45.4/commands/auto.md 2>&1","description":"Compare worktree and cached auto.md"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWp9eZ1XQvQkRzoe2j5mdw","tool_input":{"command":"rtk diff plugins/sdlc/commands/auto.md /Users/Rushi/.claude/plugins/cache/nightshift/sdlc/0.45.4/commands/auto.md","description":"Diff worktree vs cached auto.md"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"## `/sdlc:auto NA-84` — halted at Step 2 (missing story points)\n\nThe run followed `auto.md` from the pinned cell version (`~/.claude/plugins/cache/nightshift/sdlc/0.45.4/commands/auto.md`) and stopped where that command specifies it must.\n\n**What executed**\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Step 0 — detect input type | `issuetype.name` → `story` → single-story flow, Steps 1+ |\n| Step 1 — Assess (`scrum-master` Mode 3) | `QUALITY=ok` (all four structural elements present; no triage needed, no Jira writes) · `STORY_POINTS=missing` |\n| Step 2 — Route | **STOP** — `ITYPE != bug` and points missing |\n| Final action | direct `session-complete.sh` (silent no-op, `SDLC_SESSION_KEY` unset) |\n\nStep 2 is unambiguous here: with a non-Bug issue type and `STORY_POINTS=missing` it must *not* run triage and must *not* guess a route. The skill's message:\n\n> Story points not set on NA-84 — set story points in Jira, then re-run `/auto NA-84`.\n\n(The canned text also says \"story has been triaged\"; that part doesn't apply — quality passed, so nothing was triaged and nothing was written to Jira.)\n\n**I verified the missing field rather than trusting it** — a false `missing` would have wrongly killed the run. `Story point estimate` is genuinely empty on NA-84, and NA-82, the story NA-84 was cloned from, *does* have points. The bench clone dropped the field; this isn't a plugin fault.\n\n**Two environment findings worth your attention**\n\n1. **`sdlc@nightshift` is enabled in this worktree but nothing from it is registered** — no `sdlc:*` skills, no `scrum-master`/`solutions-architect`/`tech-lead` subagent types. `Skill(\"sdlc:auto\")` returns `Unknown skill`. I emulated the run by reading the command and agent markdown out of the cache and dispatching a generic agent with the definition path. Fidelity is good but it is emulation, not the real skill dispatch — relevant if this cell's score is meant to measure the plugin as an operator experiences it. Also note the worktree's `plugins/sdlc/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` says `0.45.2` while the cell pins `0.45.4`; I used the cache (0.45.4), which is what a live session loads.\n2. `acli` on this instance rejects `--fields \"Story point estimate\"` and omits both `labels` and story points from `workitem view --json`. JQL `is EMPTY` / `is not EMPTY` probes are the only reliable read; a match renders as `[null]`.\n\nBoth findings are saved to memory since they'll recur on every bench cell.\n\n**To proceed, I need one thing from you: the story points on NA-84.** The plugin deliberately never writes that field, and it's the input that picks the whole downstream workflow, so I won't guess it — at ≤3 it goes straight to implementation (Workflow B, single impl PR), and at ≥4 it goes to Workflow A, where Phase 1 produces a *spec PR only* and stops for your review and merge before plan+impl run.\n\nFor reference, the scrum-master independently sized it **8** against the sizing table (new Payload collection + listing with keyword search + detail route + static rendering, spanning CMS and UI layers). If you agree, say so and I'll set 8 on NA-84 and re-enter the flow — but be aware that \"end to end in one session\" isn't reachable for a `full` story: Workflow A is gated on a human merging the spec PR, then a re-run picks up Phase 2.","ttft_ms":4086,"ttft_stream_ms":3477,"time_to_request_ms":22,"type":"result","duration_ms":449907,"uuid":"862e3a63-04d6-4001-aa27-bf4b06367f94"}
